ot discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, genetic information, disability, pregnancy, or veteran’s status in its employment, educational programs, or benefits. As an institution of the ELCA, the College reserves the right to impose qualifications based on religion if such qualifications are related to a bona fide religious purpose or are otherwise permitted by law. Title IX Coordinator: Alli Summers Human Resources ☰ Menu About Wartburg Administration College Profile Inclusive Community Mission & Identity Photo/Video Tour of Campus Organizational Chart (PDF) The Cedar Valley Metro Waverly: Welcome Home Cedar Falls Tourism Experience Waterloo Grow Cedar Valley Employee Information (Login) Human Resources Staff Tuition Exchange Wartburg Rental Properties Get to know Waverly and the Cedar Valley. Waverly is considered part of the Waterloo/Cedar Falls metropolitan area, also called the Cedar Valley. This metro area is home to approximately 150,000 people. Learn about Waverly Address 100 Wartburg Boulevard Waverly, IA 50677 Directions & Maps Phone General 800-772-2085 Admissions 319-352-8264 Connect Facebook Instagram YouTube Search Quick Links Majors + Programs Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Studies Registrar’s Office Calendar Campus Directories My.Wartburg Give to Wartburg Knight Vision Streaming Wartburg News + Magazine The Wartburg Store Wartburg Athletics Careers at Wartburg Safety + Emergency Consumer Information Accessibility Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Copyright © Wartburg College. All rights reserved."
